		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Right way to create&amp;export collisions from Maya to Collada ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=11858#p11858"><![CDATA[
Dynamica currently creates Gimpact meshes, which are not supported by BulletColladaConverter yet. We will add support soon, for Bullet 2.74.<br><br>ColladaMaya doesn't support, export or import any physics data. Please report the issue at the ColladaMaya developers.<br><br>It is best to use Dynamica if you want to export physics information from Maya, or use the Havok tools and hkx2dae converter.<br><br>Hope this helps,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Thu Dec 18, 2008 1:29 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
